@startuml path-exact-closure-coincidence
' ============================================================================
' The coincidence counterexample of PathExactIncrementalClosure.v
' (staged_first_refuses_a_valid_delta_at_a_coincident_certificate), which
' property PX-01 builds in canonical bytes (task 11957). One namespace; numbers
' are references; paths are edge-byte lists.
'   BLUE   #1565C0  staged objects that only the target holds
'   AMBER  #EF6C00  the coincident leaf: staged, and certified at [1]
'   GREY   #607D8B  base content that is not staged
'   GREEN  #2E7D32  the corrected walk's decisions
'   RED    #C62828  the old walk's refusal
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ObjectBorderColor #455A64
skinparam NoteBorderColor #455A64

title <b>A staged leaf equal to a certified untouched leaf</b>\nthe base held content 6 under the leaf 3 at [1] and under the node C (prefix [3]) at [2];\ninserting content 7 at [2, 4] split C, and the split leaf is byte-identical to the leaf 3

object "manifest 1" as manifest #BBDEFB {
  staged
}
object "root 2" as root #BBDEFB {
  staged branch
}
object "node 4" as split #BBDEFB {
  staged branch, splits C
}
object "leaf 3" as leaf #FFE0B2 {
  empty prefix, content 6
  in the base at [1]
  staged: emitted at [2, 3]
}
object "leaf 5" as sibling #BBDEFB {
  staged, content 7
}
object "blob 7" as fresh #BBDEFB {
  staged source
}
object "blob 6" as inherited #CFD8DC {
  base only, not staged
}

manifest --> root : namespace root at []
root --> leaf : <color:#EF6C00>edge 1: occurrence at [1]</color>\n<color:#EF6C00>certified (NodeEntry, [1], 3)</color>
root --> split : edge 2: at [2]
split --> leaf : edge 3: at [2, 3]\nnot certified
split --> sibling : edge 4: at [2, 4]
sibling --> fresh : content at [2, 4]
leaf --> inherited : content at the leaf's path:\n<color:#2E7D32>certified at [2, 3] (ContentAtEndpoint)</color>\n<color:#C62828>neither staged nor certified at [1]</color>

note right of leaf #FFF3E0
  <b>Staged-first</b> (the old walk): at [1] the leaf 3 is
  staged, so the walk descends into it and reaches the
  content 6 at [1], which is neither staged nor certified
  there: <color:#C62828><b>MissingObject(6)</b></color>, for every fuel.
  ----
  <b>Certificate-first</b> (the correction): at [1] the walk
  <color:#2E7D32>stops at the exact certificate</color>; at [2, 3] it descends
  into the leaf 3 and stops at the content's certificate.
  It accepts with 8 visits and reaches 1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 3:
  the delta is valid.
end note
@enduml
